{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DDK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\etale \\to (\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\epsilon_S : (\\Sch/S)_{fppf} \\longrightarrow (\\Sch/S)_\\etale\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\epsilon_{S, *}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\epsilon_S^{-1}$", "MATH_0008": "$S_\\etale$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\pi_S : (\\Sch/S)_\\etale \\longrightarrow S_\\etale\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$S_\\etale \\to (\\Sch/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0011": "$U \\mapsto U$", "MATH_0012": "$S_\\etale$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-section-cohomology-LC}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topologies-section-change-topologies}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{topologies-section-etale}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-section-compare}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{sites-proposition-get-morphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:950479deb40687d3c1c3b628d983ad07327dc84b601334290fc311efd6cf99af", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:329c252dbab1fb10078e91cb4460530f5f19a1edb9c93484107e1bcf0e4c62b6", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nA model for this section is the section on the comparison of the\nusual topology and the qc topology on locally compact topological\nspaces as discussed in Cohomology on Sites, Section\n<REF_0001>.\nWe first review some material from\nTopologies, Sections\n<REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme and let <MATH_0002> be an fppf site.\nOn the same underlying category we have a second topology,\nnamely the <ACCENT_0001>tale topology, and hence a second site\n<MATH_0003>. The identity functor\n<MATH_0004> is continuous and defines\na morphism of sites\n<MATH_0005>\nSee Cohomology on Sites, Section <REF_0004>.\nPlease note that <MATH_0006> is the identity functor on underlying\npresheaves and that <MATH_0007> associates to an <ACCENT_0002>tale sheaf the\nfppf sheafification. Let <MATH_0008> be the small <ACCENT_0003>tale site.\nThere is a morphism of sites\n<MATH_0009>\ngiven by the continuous functor\n<MATH_0010>, <MATH_0011>.\nNamely, <MATH_0012> has fibre products and a final object and the\nfunctor above commutes with these and\nSites, Proposition <REF_0005> applies.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e81c140c5733015d410956cbc62d4d0af1be9c32e4a894c3fe332320d7b35845", "unit_id": "tag:0DDK:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DDK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$S_\\etale$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n(\\Sch/S)_{fppf} \\longrightarrow \\textit{Sets},\\quad\n(f : X \\to S) \\longmapsto \\Gamma(X, f_{small}^{-1}\\mathcal{F})\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0005": "$\\pi_S^{-1}\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\etale$", "MATH_0007": "$\\epsilon_S^{-1}\\pi_S^{-1}\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-describe-pullback-pi-fppf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cf184f705193b618f89597904f1b645bd2c80a03518c1cedfe5771bdcfd6eed7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:36a21e3f699f568400f4bd85146bcf12655db8640190c5a6a29394a3d5d31a43", "source_text": "With notation as above.\nLet <MATH_0001> be a sheaf on <MATH_0002>. The rule\n<MATH_0003>\nis a sheaf and a fortiori a sheaf on <MATH_0004>.\nIn fact this sheaf is equal to\n<MATH_0005> on <MATH_0006> and\n<MATH_0007> on <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7eccc5af24c96a02e8a91266afe604dadab562c8f5ad57d0e34be2c0288f9a47", "unit_id": "tag:0DDL:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DDK", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\pi_S^{-1}\\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-describe-pullback}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-describe-pullback}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:afc9404842b3bf549754a6ac045cbd942dacf38b2157a0d775ead112841fe232", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7119cc1428025f1bfaf1332aa588844cc4162ce6775cb2cc08065a3d7a0923c4", "source_text": "The statement about the <ACCENT_0001>tale topology is the content\nof Lemma <REF_0001>. To finish the proof it\nsuffices to show that <MATH_0001> is a sheaf for the fppf\ntopology. This is shown in Lemma <REF_0002>\nas well.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7d1f1e3ef1cd152005af1408739e3c4313f277bc74b2f9150de5b4e157c8cbe9", "unit_id": "tag:0DDL:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0DDK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\epsilon_S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\pi_S$", "MATH_0003": "$$\na_S : (\\Sch/S)_{fppf} \\longrightarrow S_\\etale\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-describe-pullback-pi-fppf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8fcade3cb77b2029dfd3f86078d1766f9d35ea1abf77b3fabc8233680a13ed5e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5a2b8ceb5233048b745bf815cd8a0f038937b5c2424ca424d4d59d8ca6b0c8d5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn the situation of Lemma <REF_0001>\nthe composition of <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> and the equality\ndetermine a morphism of sites\n<MATH_0003>\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ea288392d574611f4f44e6d4dc3bc9b5dc1297461defd66b08b2a7faca6dd025", "unit_id": "tag:0DDK:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DDK", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Sh((\\Sch/X)_{fppf}) \\ar[rr]_{f_{big, fppf}} \\ar[d]_{\\epsilon_X} & &\n\\Sh((\\Sch/Y)_{fppf}) \\ar[d]^{\\epsilon_Y} \\\\\n\\Sh((\\Sch/X)_\\etale) \\ar[rr]^{f_{big, \\etale}} & &\n\\Sh((\\Sch/Y)_\\etale)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Sh((\\Sch/X)_{fppf}) \\ar[rr]_{f_{big, fppf}} \\ar[d]_{a_X} & &\n\\Sh((\\Sch/Y)_{fppf}) \\ar[d]^{a_Y} \\\\\n\\Sh(X_\\etale) \\ar[rr]^{f_{small}} & &\n\\Sh(Y_\\etale)\n}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$a_X = \\pi_X \\circ \\epsilon_X$", "MATH_0006": "$a_Y = \\pi_X \\circ \\epsilon_X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-push-pull-fppf-etale}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:585e765f27948a39c64f60d0d7a69fa28e4c7bcfa5e1f2cbe06095da6b55c590", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d9f655f8dca46efb3ee7d12345329833715bc95b6cb29937e28138ca3b792e07", "source_text": "With notation as above.\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of <MATH_0002>.\nThen there are commutative diagrams of topoi\n<MATH_0003>\nand\n<MATH_0004>\nwith <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:83967923081662c41bf77f2262fcd1cdceb688ecbd665917652637a46683228b", "unit_id": "tag:0DDM:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DDK", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-section-change-topologies}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5660d99c39508289a0c0ca606fc9dba00b8d0eb259b4373244c005d065d95285", "source_text": "The commutativity of the diagrams follows from the discussion in\nTopologies, Section <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9434a65a1995b2f370ebbd44f6297c35c1ae0fa0597490cca759c420b729d027", "unit_id": "tag:0DDM:proof"}
